a common complaint among school voucher  and charter school advocates is that  media coverage of school choice research  is biased do they have a point to  colleagues and I examine this by  identifying five pairs of nearly  identical studies each pair measured the  same outcomes and used a same  methodology the only difference in each  case was the results  one study in each payer found a positive  result for school choice the other a  negative one we then examined major  media coverage tallying national news  stories and editorials citing each study  we found that news coverage played no  favorites coverage of positive and  negative studies was evenly balanced  editorial pages were another story  however they mention negative studies  twice as often as otherwise identical  positive ones and research was much more  likely to get mentioned by editorials  than by news coverage given this  editorial slant it's easy to see why  media coverage can feel tilted but news  coverage played it straight in this case  and that's a good thing do you think  media coverage of school choice is fair  let us know in your comments also let us  know what other topics you'd like our  scholars to cover in 60 seconds and be  sure to LIKE and subscribe for more  research and videos from AEI
 

